WEBVTT

00:01.490 --> 00:02.980
The piece you requested.

00:03.910 --> 00:06.180
I had one of our 
most skilled artisans create it.

00:07.760 --> 00:09.820
Well, this is...

00:10.920 --> 00:13.780
Yes, it is superb.

00:14.300 --> 00:16.680
If it pleases you, 
then that is all I could hope for.

00:17.260 --> 00:21.250
But are you truly certain about this? It's...

00:21.530 --> 00:26.300
About giving my granddaughter something 
so solemn in celebration of her wedding?

00:26.300 --> 00:27.210
Yes.

00:27.210 --> 00:32.220
That doesn't matter. It is the young who must 
inherit our history and carry it forward.

00:33.270 --> 00:35.680
The truth is, I did hesitate.

00:35.680 --> 00:36.590
What?

00:36.590 --> 00:39.950
What was her name? 
That girl at the exhibition.

00:39.950 --> 00:42.010
Do you mean Anne Halford?

00:42.010 --> 00:44.060
Yes, that girl.

00:44.380 --> 00:51.940
If I knew her whereabouts, then I might see 
that lovely fairy from that day once more.

00:53.410 --> 00:57.320
If you're wondering about her, 
I saw her in town a few days ago.

00:57.320 --> 00:59.050
Here in Westol?

01:00.710 --> 01:05.410
I thought it must be fate, 
so I offered to take her in here, but...

01:06.000 --> 01:07.630
Thank you, Hugh.

01:07.630 --> 01:09.380
But I won't take you up on your offer.

01:09.870 --> 01:12.670
I want to walk on my own two feet.

01:13.100 --> 01:15.790
She refused an invitation 
to the Mercury Workshop,

01:15.790 --> 01:19.640
and an offer from the Silver Sugar Viscount?

01:22.690 --> 01:24.040
How very like her.

01:24.040 --> 01:25.600
So, where is she now?

01:26.120 --> 01:29.860
Since Pull Soul Day is coming up, 
she's back in Lewiston.

01:31.160 --> 01:33.900
In that case, I may catch sight of her, too.

01:34.770 --> 01:36.670
Are you also traveling to Lewiston, my lord?

01:36.670 --> 01:40.750
Yes, there is counsel I must give the king.

01:40.750 --> 01:41.990
Counsel?

01:43.480 --> 01:45.200
The final spark.

01:45.890 --> 01:48.620
You don't mean... the Duke of Philax?

01:50.460 --> 01:58.480
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

02:05.180 --> 02:07.900
<i>It's all right</i>

02:07.900 --> 02:11.740
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

02:11.740 --> 02:18.240
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

02:18.240 --> 02:24.830
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

02:24.830 --> 02:34.140
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

02:34.590 --> 02:37.800
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

02:37.800 --> 02:40.930
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

02:41.200 --> 02:48.030
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

02:48.030 --> 02:50.730
<i>That miracle</i>

02:50.980 --> 02:57.690
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

02:57.690 --> 03:03.990
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

03:03.990 --> 03:11.110
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

03:11.110 --> 03:19.340
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

03:20.600 --> 03:23.130
Really? From Westol?

03:23.130 --> 03:25.920
Well, you've certainly chosen 
a difficult place for yourself.

03:25.920 --> 03:29.160
Since that area is under the care 
of the Silver Sugar Viscount,

03:29.160 --> 03:31.240
all your potential customers 
will have a good eye.

03:31.240 --> 03:34.900
And, in the first place, they won't deal 
with a sugar artisan from the outside.

03:35.200 --> 03:38.110
Y-You're quite knowledgeable 
about this, ma'am.

03:38.110 --> 03:41.240
You're right. I haven't had 
any customers at all.

03:41.700 --> 03:45.370
"We'll have a better chance 
in Westol," was it?

03:45.370 --> 03:46.700
Stop it, Challe!

03:46.700 --> 03:50.370
Anne may have been overly optimistic, 
but you shouldn't keep calling her stupid!

03:50.750 --> 03:53.080
I have thought it, but I haven't said it.

03:53.080 --> 03:54.920
Just now, you said it for the first time.

03:54.920 --> 03:56.050
What?

03:56.050 --> 03:58.480
If you thought it, 
that's the same as saying it!

03:58.480 --> 03:59.540
But I didn't.

03:59.540 --> 04:02.240
And even if I had called her stupid, 
why would that be bad?

04:02.240 --> 04:04.010
Because it's the truth!

04:04.010 --> 04:05.590
Hey, all of you.

04:05.900 --> 04:09.560
What's so wrong about humans 
and fairies sitting at the same table?

04:09.560 --> 04:13.670
As long as they pay, 
they're all customers to me.

04:14.200 --> 04:16.270
If you don't like it, you can leave.

04:16.270 --> 04:18.280
Honestly.

04:18.280 --> 04:19.880
But you know...

04:19.880 --> 04:23.100
it may be hard to do business 
here in Lewiston, too.

04:23.520 --> 04:26.620
After all, with Pull Soul Day, 
this is our peak season.

04:26.910 --> 04:29.440
I know, but...

04:29.440 --> 04:32.330
No, that's exactly why I have 
to work my hardest!

04:32.620 --> 04:33.920
Oh, I know!

04:33.920 --> 04:36.440
To the south of us, 
on the coast of Rockwell Province,

04:36.440 --> 04:38.490
there's a town called Philax.

04:38.490 --> 04:39.630
Have you heard of it?

04:39.980 --> 04:43.090
It's famous for trade and under the direct 
control of the royal family, isn't it?

04:43.090 --> 04:44.360
That's right!

04:44.360 --> 04:48.300
Now, about the Duke of Philax, 
Duke William Alburn...

04:49.430 --> 04:52.830
Our founding King Cedric 
left behind three family lines...

04:52.830 --> 04:57.190
House Millsland, House Chamber, 
and House Alburn.

04:57.550 --> 05:00.720
House Millsland 
are the successors to the throne,

05:00.720 --> 05:04.670
but upon the passing 
of the previous king, Edmund I,

05:04.670 --> 05:09.600
the current king, Edmund II, 
was only a twelve-year-old child.

05:09.600 --> 05:11.290
This was fifteen years ago.

05:11.820 --> 05:13.820
And, taking advantage of his age,

05:13.820 --> 05:17.610
House Chamber caused an uprising 
in an attempt to usurp the throne.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.570
It's known as the Chambers Rebellion.

05:20.570 --> 05:24.090
And you, Lord Downing, are the one 
who suppressed that rebellion...

05:24.090 --> 05:26.840
with the assistance of Thomas Alburn.

05:27.780 --> 05:32.350
To tell the truth, the events 
of that rebellion made me fear you.

05:32.940 --> 05:36.060
The ringleaders, House Chamber, 
were torn out by the roots and eradicated.

05:36.900 --> 05:40.060
Brutal is it was, let's say that 
it was understandable.

05:40.760 --> 05:44.430
But you went so far as to try 
to expel House Alburn,

05:44.430 --> 05:46.800
who aided the royal family, from the kingdom.

05:46.800 --> 05:49.530
You dismantled their military 
and even took their lands from them.

05:50.070 --> 05:52.430
That was the lesson 
learned from the rebellion.

05:52.430 --> 05:55.000
The kingdom does not need two rulers.

05:55.830 --> 05:57.610
But the current king,

05:57.610 --> 06:01.220
Edmund II, took a step back 
from your counsel...

06:01.680 --> 06:04.960
because he greatly admired 
Thomas's warm and gentle nature.

06:04.960 --> 06:09.590
His will was so strong it was difficult 
to believe that he was a twelve-year-old child.

06:10.850 --> 06:16.220
As a result, House Alburn was allotted 
land under direct royal control: Philax.

06:16.220 --> 06:18.380
Revenue must be given to the royal family,

06:18.380 --> 06:23.520
and as proof of their loyalty, 
they must visit Lewiston once a month.

06:23.520 --> 06:25.860
Those were the two conditions.

06:27.480 --> 06:29.710
And after Thomas's passing,

06:29.710 --> 06:32.910
his son William has taken on 
those conditions.

06:33.420 --> 06:35.880
I know him, personally.

06:36.330 --> 06:38.380
He has no ambition or sinister connections.

06:38.380 --> 06:40.520
He's an intelligent, gentle young man.

06:40.960 --> 06:45.630
And yet, you still call the Duke of Philax 
the last spark of rebellion?

06:46.190 --> 06:49.320
And if that spark is beginning 
to smolder once more?

06:49.750 --> 06:53.800
Soon it may start blazing again,
 raising smoke like a signal.

06:53.800 --> 06:56.860
If that isn't a spark, 
then what would you call it?

06:56.860 --> 06:57.810
Mercury?

06:59.430 --> 07:02.660
It can't be. William Alburn is...

07:03.530 --> 07:05.730
Looking for a sugar artisan?

07:05.730 --> 07:08.120
And it doesn't matter whether you're 
a silver sugar master or not.

07:08.120 --> 07:12.800
You stay at Philax Castle 
and if the duke likes the piece you made...

07:12.800 --> 07:16.330
then they say he'll pay 
a thousand cress as a reward!

07:16.330 --> 07:19.250
A-A-A thousand cress?!

07:19.250 --> 07:21.000
Shocking, isn't it?

07:21.000 --> 07:25.340
And if the Duke of Philax, a descendant of 
Ancestor King Cedric, acknowledges your skills,

07:25.340 --> 07:28.140
then you'll gain prestige as a sugar artisan.

07:28.140 --> 07:31.560
The eyes of everyone around here with 
pride in their skills lit up when they heard.

07:34.260 --> 07:35.910
A thousand cress.

07:40.240 --> 07:42.510
Philax of Rockwell Province.

07:42.510 --> 07:47.030
It flourishes through trade with the continent 
as Highland's greatest port town.

07:47.880 --> 07:52.160
But all of the money from that trade 
is swallowed up by Lewiston,

07:52.160 --> 07:56.660
and once a month, the head of the house 
must go and see how His Majesty is feeling.

07:57.180 --> 07:58.980
You know a lot about this, Challe.

07:59.420 --> 08:01.850
I haven't lived this long for nothing.

08:01.850 --> 08:04.630
I have no interest in human affairs.

08:04.990 --> 08:06.080
However...

08:07.910 --> 08:09.840
Have you brought a sugar confection?

08:09.840 --> 08:11.800
Yes. It's in my cargo hold.

08:12.110 --> 08:15.100
Good. Take your sugar 
confection and go inside.

08:15.530 --> 08:17.520
You two wait here.

08:17.520 --> 08:18.510
Open the gate!

08:25.550 --> 08:27.370
You may wait there.

08:27.370 --> 08:28.680
Oh. Yes, sir.

08:33.660 --> 08:35.160
<i>Someone arrived before me.</i>

08:35.160 --> 08:36.520
<i>Well, yes, that makes sense.</i>

08:36.520 --> 08:38.470
<i>This work can bring 
a thousand cress, after all.</i>

08:39.310 --> 08:40.870
<i>Still...</i>

08:41.370 --> 08:43.960
<i>why is this castle so bleak?</i>

08:44.460 --> 08:47.340
<i>Everything is made of stone, and somehow...</i>

08:47.340 --> 08:49.170
Hey, you.

08:49.980 --> 08:50.860
What?

08:51.450 --> 08:53.670
There is no need to bow.

08:54.470 --> 08:58.640
I am the Duke of Philax, William Alburn.

08:59.440 --> 09:01.600
Show me the sugar confections 
you have with you.

09:05.820 --> 09:07.420
You go.

09:07.420 --> 09:08.440
You stay.

09:08.440 --> 09:10.330
What? But...

09:22.200 --> 09:23.130
Good.

09:23.960 --> 09:25.560
A fairy, isn't it?

09:25.560 --> 09:27.000
Why did you make this?

09:27.470 --> 09:31.880
The model for that is one of the friends 
who is traveling with me.

09:31.880 --> 09:34.970
It was originally supposed to be 
a present for him, but...

09:34.970 --> 09:37.930
he said he didn't like it 
because it felt like cannibalism.

09:39.830 --> 09:40.810
Very well.

09:41.230 --> 09:43.140
I will allow you to stay in the castle.

09:43.830 --> 09:47.900
Make a sugar confection. 
One that satisfies my expectations.

09:48.430 --> 09:51.670
Excuse me! What sort of 
confection should I make?

09:53.320 --> 09:55.530
Oh, how beautiful!

09:56.450 --> 09:58.990
This lady... she's a fairy, isn't she?

09:59.700 --> 10:03.360
Give form to the fairy 
depicted in this portrait.

10:03.360 --> 10:04.250
Can you do it?

10:04.670 --> 10:05.450
I can!

10:06.180 --> 10:09.580
Dale, show the girl to the workshop.

10:10.280 --> 10:11.170
This way.

10:11.810 --> 10:14.130
Should you wish to view 
this portrait again...

10:14.520 --> 10:16.870
There are two towers near the workshop.

10:17.590 --> 10:23.040
In the east tower, several paintings 
of this same fairy decorate the walls.

10:23.040 --> 10:24.060
Look at those.

10:24.510 --> 10:25.270
Yes, Your Grace.

10:28.160 --> 10:31.560
A friend, huh? That was well said.

10:31.560 --> 10:34.730
The duke hates the practice 
of controlling fairies.

10:34.730 --> 10:37.440
Is that why there aren't 
any fairies in this castle?

10:38.060 --> 10:42.660
The two fairies who came with you 
have already been shown to the workshop.

10:42.660 --> 10:45.120
Oh. Thank you.

10:45.120 --> 10:49.240
I was wondering, why does the duke 
want a sugar confection of that fairy?

10:49.660 --> 10:50.620
This is it.

10:53.040 --> 10:54.750
Challe! Mithril!

10:55.100 --> 10:59.390
In that tower, there are three young 
artisans from the Radcliffe school.

10:59.390 --> 11:01.220
Make sure that none of you 
get in each others' way.

11:01.690 --> 11:03.710
Is this all there is?

11:03.710 --> 11:05.500
You saw for yourself, didn't you?

11:05.500 --> 11:09.100
There aren't many artisans 
who can live up to His Grace's eye.

11:09.100 --> 11:10.020
If that's all.

11:14.400 --> 11:16.360
A portrait of a fairy?

11:16.800 --> 11:19.320
She was an incredibly beautiful lady!

11:19.320 --> 11:22.650
And he said that there were more 
paintings of her in the east tower there.

11:22.650 --> 11:23.450
Want to go see them?

11:23.450 --> 11:25.320
If we're going anywhere, 
it's to the second floor!

11:25.320 --> 11:28.570
Did you see? There are beds 
for three people set up here!

11:28.570 --> 11:31.960
Yahoo! Bed! Bed!

11:34.760 --> 11:35.640
That was fast.

11:36.310 --> 11:37.400
Hurry up.

11:37.400 --> 11:38.050
What?

11:38.050 --> 11:40.510
The portraits. We're going 
to see them, aren't we?

11:42.120 --> 11:43.050
Let's go.

11:44.010 --> 11:45.220
Wait!

11:46.000 --> 11:49.800
I'm sorry. I didn't think 
you'd go with me, Challe.

11:49.800 --> 11:51.180
I'm just curious, that's all.

11:54.610 --> 11:56.150
Your expression is quite unrestrained.

11:56.150 --> 11:58.110
It's fine. It's because I'm happy!

12:02.410 --> 12:03.450
Jonas.

12:03.880 --> 12:04.660
Anne.

12:10.590 --> 12:12.120
What a coincidence, Jonas.

12:13.030 --> 12:15.440
Why are you here, Anne?

12:15.440 --> 12:18.090
Did you chase after me? It can't be... 
Are you here for revenge?!

12:18.660 --> 12:20.670
Revenge?

12:20.670 --> 12:21.920
Well, yes...

12:21.920 --> 12:23.660
that wouldn't be bad,

12:23.660 --> 12:25.520
but I don't have that much time on my hands.

12:25.520 --> 12:26.740
Hey, wait.

12:27.630 --> 12:31.210
Jonas, this is that woman 
from the exhibition, isn't it?

12:31.210 --> 12:34.310
Th-That's right! She's the one who set me up!

12:34.310 --> 12:35.280
What?

12:35.280 --> 12:37.600
When am I supposed to have set you up?

12:37.600 --> 12:39.790
You're the one who resorted to cowardly methods!

12:39.790 --> 12:41.870
No, I saw it.

12:41.870 --> 12:45.860
You're the one who said that 
you made the piece Jonas entered.

12:46.480 --> 12:50.450
That soured the king's mood, 
and the Royal Medal was no more.

12:50.860 --> 12:55.920
As fellow members of the Radcliffe school, 
we can't let this quietly pass.

12:55.920 --> 12:58.120
Then, what will you do?

12:59.700 --> 13:01.630
I am asking you what you will do.

13:03.430 --> 13:06.570
I'm sure you came here after 
hearing word of the Duke of Philax,

13:06.570 --> 13:08.960
but the glory and reward belong to me!

13:08.960 --> 13:10.600
Work as hard as you want.

13:10.600 --> 13:12.560
I won't lose in a contest of skill!

13:12.860 --> 13:15.560
You're the one who should hurry up 
and start preparing to go home!

13:16.180 --> 13:17.370
Honestly!

13:17.370 --> 13:19.230
All right, Scarecrow.

13:19.610 --> 13:20.690
Are we doing this?

13:21.570 --> 13:22.650
Yes.

13:56.020 --> 13:57.390
Is it finished?

13:57.390 --> 13:58.650
Just a little more.

13:59.020 --> 14:02.890
Thank you, Mithril Lid Pod. 
You've really been so much help!

14:02.890 --> 14:06.750
When the greatness that is I makes a serious 
effort, this is how much help I can be!

14:06.750 --> 14:09.230
Though it isn't nearly enough 
to return the favor yet.

14:09.230 --> 14:11.740
You don't need to worry about 
returning the favor anymore.

14:12.220 --> 14:15.770
Still, where has that Challe gone?

14:15.770 --> 14:18.970
Every time you start work, 
he wanders off somewhere.

14:18.970 --> 14:22.840
Though, apparently even that guy 
can wallow in sentimentality sometimes.

14:22.840 --> 14:24.800
Sentimentality? Challe?

14:25.120 --> 14:29.950
Three days ago, when we came here, 
we had to wait outside, right?

14:29.950 --> 14:31.010
It was back then.

14:31.700 --> 14:33.010
How nostalgic.

14:33.010 --> 14:33.720
What is?

14:34.740 --> 14:37.680
Long ago, I lived in a castle like this one.

14:38.160 --> 14:40.120
Challe? In a castle?

14:41.720 --> 14:43.740
<i>That girl was Liz...</i>

14:43.740 --> 14:45.690
<i>Her name was Elizabeth.</i>

14:46.330 --> 14:49.390
<i>Could he have meant 
that person named Liz and he...</i>

14:49.390 --> 14:52.240
Anne! The tip of your nose is all blue!

14:51.840 --> 14:52.780
What?

14:52.240 --> 14:54.030
There's pigment powder all over your face!

14:54.030 --> 14:55.150
How is that?

14:55.150 --> 14:56.700
You're even more blue now!

14:56.700 --> 14:59.710
What? I-I'm just going to go 
and wash my face!

15:05.810 --> 15:08.270
<i>Fifteen years passed.</i>

15:08.270 --> 15:10.760
<i>Liz's hair turned a pale gold...</i>

15:10.760 --> 15:12.350
<i>her freckles disappeared...</i>

15:12.350 --> 15:14.070
<i>and she became a beautiful young woman.</i>

15:14.960 --> 15:16.170
<i>That's why I know.</i>

15:16.640 --> 15:18.890
<i>You will continue to change, just as Liz did.</i>

15:19.750 --> 15:21.240
<i>Will I change?</i>

15:22.130 --> 15:24.170
<i>I can't imagine that I will.</i>

15:24.170 --> 15:28.900
<i>I'll stay like this, scrawny 
and gangly, like a scarecrow.</i>

15:29.360 --> 15:32.170
<i>I wonder what kind of person Liz was.</i>

15:32.170 --> 15:34.570
<i>I'm sure she must have been beautiful.</i>

15:34.900 --> 15:38.340
<i>After all, someone as beautiful 
as Challe calls her beautiful.</i>

15:39.580 --> 15:41.180
What is this? Am I jealous?

15:41.180 --> 15:43.050
Of a woman I've never met?

15:43.050 --> 15:44.730
How ridiculous can I be?

15:45.360 --> 15:47.580
If you rub that hard, 
your nose will come off.

15:48.000 --> 15:48.960
Challe...

15:49.530 --> 15:50.670
Your clothes will get wet.

15:51.160 --> 15:51.940
What?

15:52.600 --> 15:53.640
Oh.

15:53.640 --> 15:55.390
I forgot to bring something 
to dry myself with.

16:03.680 --> 16:04.400
What's wrong?

16:04.400 --> 16:06.090
Huh? Nothing...

16:06.530 --> 16:07.690
Um...

16:07.690 --> 16:08.740
Scarecrow?

16:11.820 --> 16:14.170
It-It's nothing!

16:16.130 --> 16:16.990
Jonas?

16:18.800 --> 16:20.160
What is it?

16:20.160 --> 16:23.960
If you're looking for a sugar 
confection to steal, it isn't done yet.

16:24.280 --> 16:28.720
How could you think that? 
I have no need of your sugar confection.

16:28.720 --> 16:31.550
I finished my piece yesterday.

16:31.550 --> 16:32.920
So did the other two.

16:33.320 --> 16:37.390
Really. So, did His Grace view them?

16:37.710 --> 16:41.720
Of course! And what do you think happened?

16:42.730 --> 16:45.370
The other two were told to leave!

16:45.370 --> 16:49.040
I was the <i>only</i> one permitted 
to stay here at the castle.

16:49.040 --> 16:52.440
When he saw my piece, His Grace said this.

16:52.440 --> 16:55.440
"It shows promise. 
Increase the level of accuracy."

16:55.440 --> 17:00.410
Sorry, Anne, but the one who will 
receive the thousand cress will be <i>me</i>!

17:00.410 --> 17:01.870
Th-That hasn't been decided—

17:01.370 --> 17:02.940
Did you know?

17:02.940 --> 17:09.320
They say I'm the <i>first</i> one allowed to stay in the castle after showing a piece.

17:09.320 --> 17:12.840
I'm the <i>only</i> one. That's what Dale said.

17:12.840 --> 17:14.220
Well, I'm going to—

17:14.220 --> 17:15.200
It's no use.

17:15.680 --> 17:18.640
I'm moving to that tower.

17:18.640 --> 17:21.390
It's a privilege of the chosen artisan.

17:21.740 --> 17:25.890
The rootless, wandering artisan should 
go ahead and try her best right here.

17:26.300 --> 17:28.970
What was he trying to achieve by coming here?

17:28.970 --> 17:31.450
Was it some scheme to try 
to whittle away at my motivation?

17:31.450 --> 17:34.330
It's likely that he simply wanted to brag.

17:34.330 --> 17:35.110
Challe...

17:36.020 --> 17:39.370
After all, he can't brag to 
those allies of his who are leaving.

17:39.760 --> 17:41.330
What is wrong with him?

17:45.000 --> 17:46.420
It's finished!

17:46.420 --> 17:47.500
I think.

17:48.440 --> 17:50.960
What do you think, Challe? 
Will you look at it for me?

17:53.170 --> 17:54.630
It's well made.

17:55.360 --> 17:55.920
Hey.

18:19.490 --> 18:22.540
You did well, Scarecrow.

18:41.170 --> 18:42.010
It's not right.

18:42.480 --> 18:44.220
<i>It didn't please him.</i>

18:46.400 --> 18:49.040
But the feel is exactly right.

18:49.040 --> 18:49.730
What?

18:50.470 --> 18:52.680
The feel of it is better than his.

18:53.210 --> 18:56.940
Increase the level of accuracy 
so that you might satisfy me.

18:57.860 --> 18:59.910
Move to this tower immediately.

19:00.510 --> 19:02.060
We have two artisans.

19:02.520 --> 19:05.200
There is no need to increase 
their number any further.

19:08.140 --> 19:09.100
Come.

19:12.350 --> 19:18.050
Um, does this mean that His Grace 
was pleased with my sugar confection?

19:18.590 --> 19:21.360
Let's say that he found it not entirely bad.

19:21.360 --> 19:24.460
You and... Jonas Anders, was it?

19:24.960 --> 19:28.270
He has entrusted the making of 
the piece to the two of you, after all.

19:28.600 --> 19:30.620
I've dispatched pages.

19:30.620 --> 19:33.600
Your fairies should be here soon.

19:33.600 --> 19:35.860
I'll have your things brought later.

19:35.860 --> 19:38.260
Th-Thank you.

19:38.760 --> 19:40.320
<i>Not entirely bad?</i>

19:40.600 --> 19:42.780
There are two meals, morning and evening.

19:42.780 --> 19:45.530
You may use as much silver sugar as you like.

19:45.530 --> 19:47.290
We will prepare anything you need.

19:47.760 --> 19:50.250
Should you find that 
you require anything else...

19:50.680 --> 19:52.440
just pull this cord.

19:52.910 --> 19:57.500
It will ring a bell in the servants' quarters 
and let us know that we're needed.

19:57.500 --> 20:00.600
Then, when I've finished the piece...

20:00.600 --> 20:02.410
Naturally, that will be this cord as well.

20:02.910 --> 20:04.520
Do you have any other questions?

20:04.520 --> 20:06.970
Why are you here?!

20:07.310 --> 20:10.400
I thought I heard something above me and...

20:10.400 --> 20:12.440
Tell me! Why, Anne?

20:12.960 --> 20:16.730
Why do you suppose? 
I've been told to move here.

20:16.730 --> 20:18.220
That can't be!

20:18.730 --> 20:21.880
So you two know each other.

20:21.880 --> 20:24.540
I don't know how your fates 
may be intertwined,

20:24.540 --> 20:28.200
but whatever the case, this is 
something that His Grace has decided.

20:32.930 --> 20:35.250
I have to compete against you again?

20:35.250 --> 20:38.210
If you insist that the exhibition 
was a competition, then yes!

20:39.490 --> 20:42.460
You... You're nothing that I can't...

20:42.460 --> 20:45.280
The likes of you will never 
measure up to Master Jonas!

20:45.280 --> 20:46.010
Cathy!

20:46.360 --> 20:47.790
Right, Master Jonas?

20:47.790 --> 20:49.450
W-Well, yes.

20:50.440 --> 20:52.480
I'll never lose to someone like you!

20:52.860 --> 20:54.440
I won't lose either.

20:54.950 --> 20:56.870
I won't <i>ever</i> be beaten!

20:59.190 --> 21:04.950
The Castle on the Sea

21:16.210 --> 21:20.540
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.410 --> 21:26.680
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.680 --> 21:30.220
<i>Just as our night dreams are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.220 --> 21:37.290
<i>If they aren't held dear, they will disappear?</i>

21:37.290 --> 21:48.430
<i>No, it's because they aren't things that only special people can see</i>

21:48.430 --> 21:49.160
<i>That day</i>

21:49.160 --> 21:53.610
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.610 --> 21:59.170
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.170 --> 22:04.670
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.670 --> 22:08.970
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:08.970 --> 22:14.800
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.800 --> 22:26.280
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.080 --> 22:40.000
<b>A False Farewell</b>
